  "review": {
    "entityID": "person:israel_682",
    "book": "ROM",
    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "Romans 9:4 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "who are Israelites; whose is the adoption, the glory, the covenants, the giving of the law, the service, and the promises;"
      },
      {
        "ref": "Romans 9:6 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "But it is not as though the word of God has come to nothing. For they are not all Israel that are of Israel."
      },
      {
        "ref": "Romans 9:13 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Even as it is written, “Jacob I loved, but Esau I hated.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "Romans 9:27 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Isaiah cries concerning Israel, “If the number of the children of Israel are as the sand of the sea, it is the remnant who will be saved;"
      },
      {
        "ref": "Romans 9:31 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "but Israel, following after a law of righteousness, didn’t arrive at the law of righteousness."
      },
      {
        "ref": "Romans 10:1 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "Brothers, my heart’s desire and my prayer to God is for Israel, that they may be saved."
      },
      {
        "ref": "Romans 10:19 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "But I ask, didn’t Israel know? First Moses says, “I will provoke you to jealousy with that which is no nation. I will make you angry with a nation void of understanding.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "Romans 10:21 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "But about Israel he says, “All day long I stretched out my hands to a disobedient and contrary people.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "Romans 11:1 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "I ask then, did God reject his people? May it never be! For I also am an Israelite, a descendant of Abraham, of the tribe of Benjamin."
      },
      {
        "ref": "Romans 11:2 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "God didn’t reject his people, whom he foreknew. Or don’t you know what the Scripture says about Elijah? How he pleads with God against Israel:"
      },
      {
        "ref": "Romans 11:7 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "What then? That which Israel seeks for, that he didn’t obtain, but the chosen ones obtained it, and the rest were hardened."
      },
      {
        "ref": "Romans 11:25 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "For I don’t desire you to be ignorant, brothers, of this mystery, so that you won’t be wise in your own conceits, that a partial hardening has happened to Israel, until the fullness of the Gentiles has come in,"
      },
      {
        "ref": "Romans 11:26 (WEB)",
        "textualBasisJa": "and so all Israel will be saved. Even as it is written, “There will come out of Zion the Deliverer, and he will turn away ungodliness from Jacob."
      }
    ],
